    "title": "A=1 core-free pole-slack exclusion",
    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "adaptive pole interpolation and three-contact vanishing",
    "statement": "For a failing core-free A=1 profile, let ell=4e-T and let p be the actual pole-ideal colength. Set alpha=2 for e<=rho/2-1, alpha=1 for rho/2<=e<=rho-1, and alpha=0 for e=rho. The profile is impossible whenever floor(p/(alpha+1))+ell+3<e. Every survivor therefore has p>=(alpha+1)(e-ell-3). At the first live degree e=m+1 only ell=0,1,2 remain, with pole deficiency Delta-p at most 5,8,11 respectively.",
